1
00:00:08,008 --> 00:00:10,052
[Hsiu-wen] <i>It's okay. Leave
the documents on my desk.</i>

2
00:00:11,011 --> 00:00:12,513
Fine. Set up a meeting

3
00:00:12,638 --> 00:00:14,473
with the three branch managers
in Zhongshan District.

4
00:00:15,307 --> 00:00:18,643
<i>It has been ten years
since I last saw Lu-yung.</i>

5
00:00:18,644 --> 00:00:22,231
<i>After graduation
from grad school,
I filled my life with work.</i>

6
00:00:22,814 --> 00:00:26,609
<i>Just when he was gradually
fading from my memory,</i>

7
00:00:26,610 --> 00:00:29,488
<i>Chou Lu-yung realized
that seemingly unrealistic
dream of his</i>

8
00:00:29,613 --> 00:00:31,490
<i>from when he was 19.</i>

9
00:00:35,202 --> 00:00:37,663
JIN LAI HAO

10
00:00:37,788 --> 00:00:40,832
[soft dramatic music playing]

11
00:00:55,389 --> 00:00:56,515
[Lu-yung] Wu Hsiu-wen?

12
00:01:01,645 --> 00:01:03,188
Lu-yung.

13
00:01:13,365 --> 00:01:15,367
<i>You know, some people</i>

14
00:01:15,492 --> 00:01:18,744
<i>will never, ever change.</i>

15
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:21,331
[music continues]

16
00:01:36,388 --> 00:01:38,390
[both laugh]

17
00:01:41,893 --> 00:01:43,770
It's been ten years.

18
00:01:43,895 --> 00:01:45,522
You haven't changed at all.

19
00:01:46,648 --> 00:01:48,482
Yes, I have.

20
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:50,110
I've got crow's feet.

21
00:01:50,694 --> 00:01:52,779
- I did see a couple of them.
- And I see your freckles.

22
00:01:52,904 --> 00:01:54,573
[laughter]

23
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:01,746
Are you almost ready
to open the new Jin Lai Hao?

24
00:02:01,747 --> 00:02:02,873
Yeah.

25
00:02:04,458 --> 00:02:06,459
Hopefully, I won't bring
shame to my dad's name.

26
00:02:06,460 --> 00:02:08,128
No, you won't.

27
00:02:08,253 --> 00:02:11,548
The Chou Lu-yung I know
can do whatever he wants to do.

28
00:02:14,426 --> 00:02:15,552
Really?

29
00:02:16,678 --> 00:02:18,639
- Am I that good?
- Yeah.

30
00:02:20,265 --> 00:02:22,517
You're better than you think.

31
00:02:24,895 --> 00:02:26,521
[chuckles]

32
00:02:32,402 --> 00:02:33,445
How about you?

33
00:02:35,405 --> 00:02:37,199
Why didn't you study abroad?

34
00:02:39,284 --> 00:02:40,701
I wanted to.

35
00:02:40,702 --> 00:02:42,496
I even got a job in London.

36
00:02:44,873 --> 00:02:46,583
But life is always changing.

37
00:02:48,418 --> 00:02:49,836
It's a long story.

38
00:02:49,961 --> 00:02:51,879
Anyway, I stayed and ended up
working for Chang Xin.

39
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:52,964
I'm still there.

40
00:02:56,343 --> 00:02:57,427
You know.

41
00:03:02,182 --> 00:03:04,308
If that was your decision,

42
00:03:04,309 --> 00:03:07,396
I believe everything
will get better.

43
00:03:11,441 --> 00:03:13,235
- Let's work hard.
- Okay.

44
00:03:13,819 --> 00:03:15,320
[chuckles]

45
00:03:19,950 --> 00:03:21,535
Will we become rivals?

46
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:26,790
You'll never be my rival.

47
00:03:29,584 --> 00:03:32,629
[music continues]

48
00:03:41,304 --> 00:03:45,599
[singer] <i>♪ Someday, you can
Find sunshine, sunshine ♪</i>

49
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:50,188
[singing in Mandarin]

50
00:03:50,313 --> 00:03:52,440
<i>♪ Run, run, to hope ♪</i>

51
00:03:52,441 --> 00:03:54,525
<i>♪ Hope, hope, don't go ♪</i>

52
00:03:54,526 --> 00:03:56,570
<i>♪ I believe in you someday ♪</i>

53
00:03:56,695 --> 00:03:58,779
[singing in Mandarin]

54
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:02,743
<i>♪ Someone just like you
Lights up my dream ♪</i>

55
00:04:02,868 --> 00:04:06,872
[singing in Mandarin]

56
00:04:11,376 --> 00:04:14,379
[tense music playing]

57
00:04:19,968 --> 00:04:22,262
Take your time. [laughs]

58
00:04:31,521 --> 00:04:35,233
Last time, you said you felt
like you had sand in your eye.

59
00:04:35,358 --> 00:04:37,569
I want to get it out.

60
00:04:39,571 --> 00:04:40,821
I want to expand.

61
00:04:40,822 --> 00:04:42,531
Why don't we take a risk
and go big all at once?

62
00:04:42,532 --> 00:04:45,743
Jin Lai Hao has got
only one restaurant now.

63
00:04:45,744 --> 00:04:48,455
What if we purchase
their storefront?

64
00:04:49,456 --> 00:04:50,957
How do you think they'd be?

65
00:04:53,043 --> 00:04:55,461
It's not right.

66
00:04:55,462 --> 00:04:57,464
You're so mean.

67
00:04:58,507 --> 00:05:00,008
You're forcing them
to kill themselves?

68
00:05:02,761 --> 00:05:04,930
[laughing]

69
00:05:12,479 --> 00:05:15,774
Hsiu-wen, Chang Xin
can't live without you.

70
00:05:17,067 --> 00:05:18,819
[chuckles] Thank you, sir.

71
00:05:26,910 --> 00:05:28,537
I hope you can understand.

72
00:05:31,414 --> 00:05:32,707
If this is your decision,

73
00:05:34,084 --> 00:05:35,669
just be yourself.

74
00:05:41,424 --> 00:05:42,968
What are you doing, Yi-hsuan?

75
00:05:44,719 --> 00:05:48,473
She wants us to have nothing.
And you still care about her?

76
00:05:55,105 --> 00:05:58,024
I just want to protect
our restaurant.

77
00:05:58,149 --> 00:06:01,611
[soft dramatic music playing]

78
00:06:14,124 --> 00:06:16,001
Can I take a look
at your equipment?

79
00:06:20,964 --> 00:06:22,048
Yeah.

80
00:06:23,508 --> 00:06:24,968
Be our guest.

81
00:06:32,642 --> 00:06:34,019
[Feng] Let's have a smoke.

82
00:06:35,896 --> 00:06:38,106
[music continues]

83
00:06:43,695 --> 00:06:44,988
[cell phone ringing]

84
00:06:48,867 --> 00:06:49,951
Lu-yung?

85
00:06:54,539 --> 00:06:56,541
Chairman Chang wants
to talk to you.

86
00:06:56,666 --> 00:06:58,460
[tense music playing]

87
00:07:20,982 --> 00:07:22,484
You're here.

88
00:07:25,570 --> 00:07:27,614
I think you know your plight.

89
00:07:32,661 --> 00:07:36,873
But your dishes
that I ate last time

90
00:07:38,208 --> 00:07:41,086
reminded me of your dad.

91
00:07:44,172 --> 00:07:47,550
I can help you
standardize your recipes

92
00:07:50,887 --> 00:07:54,099
so that more people
can taste your dad's cooking.

93
00:07:54,224 --> 00:07:56,893
- How's that?
- I'll never say yes to that.

94
00:07:58,520 --> 00:08:01,856
Don't hasten to say no.
I haven't given you my offer.

95
00:08:04,067 --> 00:08:06,110
If you say yes,

96
00:08:06,111 --> 00:08:09,114
maybe I'll consider to keep
leasing the storefront to you.

97
00:08:09,239 --> 00:08:10,532
How's that?

98
00:08:17,622 --> 00:08:19,666
I'll never sell you
any one of my dishes.

99
00:08:21,126 --> 00:08:22,961
Thank you for your time today.

100
00:08:24,504 --> 00:08:25,588
Chou Lu-yung?

101
00:08:29,843 --> 00:08:31,261
[sighs]

102
00:08:31,511 --> 00:08:33,887
I'm giving you a chance
for your dad's sake.

103
00:08:33,888 --> 00:08:36,682
But I need you to know.

104
00:08:36,683 --> 00:08:38,892
As long as you stay in Taiwan,

105
00:08:38,893 --> 00:08:40,186
believe it or not,

106
00:08:41,813 --> 00:08:43,481
with my capability,

107
00:08:43,606 --> 00:08:46,985
I can purchase
all the storefronts
that you lease, one by one.

108
00:08:49,654 --> 00:08:50,905
What exactly do you want?

109
00:08:51,990 --> 00:08:53,658
[sighs]

110
00:08:53,783 --> 00:08:57,787
An impulsive decision
will absolutely do us no good.

111
00:08:59,330 --> 00:09:01,248
You run a business now.

112
00:09:01,249 --> 00:09:03,334
Think clearly.

113
00:09:09,174 --> 00:09:11,217
Do us no good?

114
00:09:11,342 --> 00:09:12,885
You mean money-wise?

115
00:09:12,886 --> 00:09:16,806
The problem between us
can't be solved with money.

116
00:09:24,564 --> 00:09:26,566
If you don't own a restaurant,

117
00:09:28,234 --> 00:09:31,905
maybe your friends will
leave you one after another.

118
00:09:33,907 --> 00:09:37,702
I own a restaurant
because they trust me.

119
00:09:37,827 --> 00:09:39,871
They're different from you.

120
00:09:42,123 --> 00:09:43,875
It's your last chance.

121
00:09:44,918 --> 00:09:46,628
Don't regret it.

122
00:09:52,050 --> 00:09:53,885
What I want
is actually very simple.

123
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:59,098
You and Chang Chien-yuan
will turn yourselves
in to the police

124
00:09:59,099 --> 00:10:01,058
and apologize to me and my dad.

125
00:10:01,059 --> 00:10:02,893
[rock music playing]

126
00:10:02,894 --> 00:10:05,939
[singer singing in Mandarin]

127
00:10:28,211 --> 00:10:29,295
[music ends]

128
00:10:52,068 --> 00:10:53,944
Hey, lady, are you by yourself?

129
00:10:53,945 --> 00:10:56,072
[light music playing]

130
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:59,159
Let's chat.

131
00:10:59,284 --> 00:11:02,120
Come on!

132
00:11:03,413 --> 00:11:05,956
The cocktail tastes good.

133
00:11:05,957 --> 00:11:09,252
Of course. I made it for you
to cure your depression.

134
00:11:16,968 --> 00:11:18,970
You came to work
at our restaurant

135
00:11:19,095 --> 00:11:22,055
because you had a crush
on our boss, didn't you?

136
00:11:22,056 --> 00:11:23,141
So what?

137
00:11:24,309 --> 00:11:27,687
If he's someone
who only cares about profit,

138
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:29,354
and will do whatever it takes,

139
00:11:29,355 --> 00:11:31,149
would you still love him?

140
00:11:32,692 --> 00:11:34,944
What do you want to tell me?

141
00:11:36,821 --> 00:11:38,448
You know his past, don't you?

142
00:11:38,698 --> 00:11:42,952
He has to take a different
path from Chang Da-chin
to prove himself,

143
00:11:43,828 --> 00:11:45,245
to make it all mean something.

144
00:11:45,246 --> 00:11:48,207
[emotional music playing]

145
00:11:48,208 --> 00:11:50,835
So, it'll be really
hard for him.

146
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:53,838
Watching from the sideline,
it breaks our hearts.

147
00:11:55,131 --> 00:11:57,508
He's stubborn as hell.

148
00:11:57,759 --> 00:12:00,386
Yeah. And nobody can change him.

149
00:12:01,804 --> 00:12:06,476
So, if you choose to side with
him, don't try to change him.

150
00:12:06,726 --> 00:12:09,103
But get ready
to walk on with him.

151
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:16,444
Try to understand him, girl.

152
00:12:17,904 --> 00:12:19,863
Try to understand?

153
00:12:19,864 --> 00:12:22,866
It sounds like I need
one more drink.

154
00:12:22,867 --> 00:12:25,118
You want one more? Okay.

155
00:12:25,119 --> 00:12:26,955
Maybe I'll make you...

156
00:12:28,164 --> 00:12:31,041
a "Lovestruck Girl".

157
00:12:31,042 --> 00:12:33,878
- A lovestruck girl. Yeah.
- A lovestruck girl.

158
00:12:34,003 --> 00:12:36,547
- A lovestruck girl.
- It's you. Wake up!

159
00:12:36,798 --> 00:12:41,803
- A lovestruck girl.
- A lovestruck girl.

160
00:12:45,556 --> 00:12:47,933
[indistinct chatter]

161
00:12:47,934 --> 00:12:50,186
But didn't we confirm it
the other day?

162
00:12:55,441 --> 00:12:57,276
[Feng] Be careful.

163
00:12:57,277 --> 00:12:58,944
It's heavy.

164
00:12:58,945 --> 00:13:00,445
[Lu-yung] Got it. Thanks.

165
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:02,239
[Feng] Lend a hand.

166
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:05,284
- Any more left inside?
- [Yu-li] I'll take this one.
Here.

167
00:13:05,285 --> 00:13:07,453
- The landlord changed his mind.
- Huh?

168
00:13:07,578 --> 00:13:09,080
[Chin-nan] Again?

169
00:13:09,789 --> 00:13:11,999
Damn! It's the fifth one!

170
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,085
How is this possible?

171
00:13:14,210 --> 00:13:17,588
How rich are they exactly?
They've purchased
wherever we tried to rent.

172
00:13:17,839 --> 00:13:19,464
Here's the deal.

173
00:13:19,465 --> 00:13:21,341
We'll rent random places
for them to purchase
until they go bankrupt.

174
00:13:21,342 --> 00:13:24,011
But they don't have to purchase.
They're just trying to stall us.

175
00:13:24,012 --> 00:13:25,805
We're the ones in a hurry here,
not them.

176
00:13:27,223 --> 00:13:29,976
How about we move
to another city?

177
00:13:30,101 --> 00:13:32,144
No use. They'll deliberately
cause us trouble.

178
00:13:32,145 --> 00:13:33,980
Wherever we go, they can do it.

179
00:13:34,105 --> 00:13:35,355
[Chin-nan] Here's the deal.

180
00:13:35,356 --> 00:13:37,316
Get the boys and weapons.
It's war!

181
00:13:37,317 --> 00:13:39,277
Hey, we need constructive ideas.

182
00:13:41,529 --> 00:13:42,947
Just kidding.

183
00:13:50,246 --> 00:13:52,164
I have an idea.

184
00:13:52,165 --> 00:13:54,542
[pensive music playing]

185
00:13:55,835 --> 00:13:56,919
Tell us.

186
00:13:58,921 --> 00:14:02,633
I'm thinking
we try a food truck.

187
00:14:02,884 --> 00:14:04,010
A food truck?

188
00:14:04,135 --> 00:14:06,304
You mean,
like an ice cream truck?

189
00:14:06,429 --> 00:14:09,474
He wants to play games.
Let's not face him head-on.

190
00:14:09,599 --> 00:14:11,516
As long as we keep the brand
of Jin Lai Hao alive,

191
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:13,560
we stand a chance.

192
00:14:13,561 --> 00:14:16,229
But with a food truck,
it means guerrilla warfare
in the kitchen.

193
00:14:16,230 --> 00:14:18,482
But we're a Taiwan-style bistro.

194
00:14:18,483 --> 00:14:20,400
- This is...
- So we'll need to simplify.

195
00:14:20,401 --> 00:14:23,528
How do you simplify
Taiwanese cuisine?

196
00:14:23,529 --> 00:14:25,405
This is just temporary.

197
00:14:25,406 --> 00:14:29,160
As long as our brand name
is still visible,
we stand a chance.

198
00:14:29,285 --> 00:14:30,661
Simplifying Taiwanese cuisine...

199
00:14:36,626 --> 00:14:37,919
Braised pork rice?

200
00:14:41,172 --> 00:14:45,092
I'm confident
in my braised pork rice.

201
00:14:45,093 --> 00:14:47,178
They've tried it.
It tastes good.

202
00:14:47,303 --> 00:14:49,388
If braised pork works,

203
00:14:49,389 --> 00:14:53,558
it can go with noodles,
or rice, or basically
anything as a sauce.

204
00:14:53,559 --> 00:14:54,560
It's simple.

205
00:14:54,685 --> 00:14:56,521
I think it's a good idea.

206
00:14:56,646 --> 00:14:58,648
There are many variations.

207
00:14:58,898 --> 00:15:02,026
Speaking of variations,
maybe we pair them
with my cocktails.

208
00:15:02,151 --> 00:15:04,444
Braise pork or fried food
with Long Island Iced Tea.

209
00:15:04,445 --> 00:15:06,446
I love Long Island Iced Tea.

210
00:15:06,447 --> 00:15:08,573
Leave the truck to me.

211
00:15:08,574 --> 00:15:10,660
Hey. You can't steal one.

212
00:15:11,619 --> 00:15:12,703
No, I won't.

213
00:15:14,497 --> 00:15:16,624
[reverberating sound]

214
00:15:19,544 --> 00:15:23,548
[singer] <i>♪ Nobody knows ♪</i>

215
00:15:23,673 --> 00:15:26,591
<i>♪ Nobody, nobody knows me ♪</i>

216
00:15:26,592 --> 00:15:29,095
- That's it then.
- [Feng] Are you serious?

217
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:31,263
Cool!

218
00:15:31,264 --> 00:15:32,598
Come to my place
for the preparation and tasting.

219
00:15:32,723 --> 00:15:34,225
Okay?

220
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:39,563
[singer] <i>♪ Hold on, whoa ♪</i>

221
00:15:39,564 --> 00:15:43,734
<i>♪ Hold on, whoa ♪</i>

222
00:15:43,985 --> 00:15:45,444
<i>♪ Hold on... ♪</i>

223
00:15:45,445 --> 00:15:46,571
[Yi-hsuan] Here goes.

224
00:15:46,696 --> 00:15:47,697
Jin Lai Hao.

225
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:49,365
- Jin Lai Hao.
- Go!

226
00:15:51,242 --> 00:15:52,410
One more time.

227
00:16:06,674 --> 00:16:07,967
Spot on.

228
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:11,636
Spot on.

229
00:16:11,637 --> 00:16:14,682
[upbeat music playing]

230
00:16:20,104 --> 00:16:22,356
That thin?
They might be blown away.

231
00:16:24,108 --> 00:16:25,776
Cut them thicker
for some texture.

232
00:16:28,321 --> 00:16:29,405
Yes, sir!

233
00:16:30,698 --> 00:16:33,325
[singer] <i>♪ Nobody knows ♪</i>

234
00:16:33,326 --> 00:16:35,786
<i>♪ Nobody, nobody knows me ♪</i>

235
00:16:36,037 --> 00:16:38,456
<i>♪ Nobody knows ♪</i>

236
00:16:38,581 --> 00:16:41,291
<i>♪ Nobody, nobody knows me ♪</i>

237
00:16:41,292 --> 00:16:44,462
[singer vocalizing]

238
00:16:52,303 --> 00:16:54,305
<i>♪ Waiting for you... ♪</i>

239
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:57,390
<i>♪ Nobody, nobody knows me ♪</i>

240
00:16:57,391 --> 00:16:59,476
<i>♪ Waiting for you... ♪</i>

241
00:16:59,477 --> 00:17:02,480
<i>♪ Nobody, nobody knows me ♪</i>

242
00:17:02,605 --> 00:17:04,023
<i>♪ Waiting for you... ♪</i>

243
00:17:04,148 --> 00:17:05,357
Say something.

244
00:17:05,358 --> 00:17:07,318
Whether it's good or not,
just tell me.

245
00:17:08,361 --> 00:17:09,486
Smells good!

246
00:17:09,487 --> 00:17:11,154
[excited grunts]

247
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:12,281
Tastes good!

248
00:17:13,282 --> 00:17:15,701
- So good that I'm gonna cry.
- It's good, huh?

249
00:17:15,826 --> 00:17:18,287
- You're exaggerating.
- It's true.

250
00:17:19,705 --> 00:17:21,040
It tastes...

251
00:17:21,165 --> 00:17:22,208
good enough.

252
00:17:23,334 --> 00:17:24,710
But that's just the basics.

253
00:17:26,254 --> 00:17:30,216
We need to present it
in a different style.

254
00:17:31,551 --> 00:17:33,261
[Lu-yung]
I love the braised pork.

255
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:36,430
Let's think about
how customers take it to go.

256
00:17:37,515 --> 00:17:40,059
[Chin-nan] I want the whole pot.

257
00:17:40,184 --> 00:17:41,686
The best braised pork ever.
Got my respect.

258
00:17:41,811 --> 00:17:44,187
[Yu-li]
What are you talking about?

259
00:17:44,188 --> 00:17:46,399
[Chin-nan] Listen to me.
This is a winner.

260
00:17:46,524 --> 00:17:49,277
[singer vocalizing]

261
00:17:52,572 --> 00:17:54,115
You got into business school.

262
00:17:54,699 --> 00:17:56,449
Here.

263
00:17:56,450 --> 00:18:00,537
Go to New York
two months before school starts

264
00:18:00,538 --> 00:18:02,622
to get familiar
with the surroundings.

265
00:18:02,623 --> 00:18:04,709
If you need anything,
call me anytime.

266
00:18:10,339 --> 00:18:11,424
Dad...

267
00:18:12,758 --> 00:18:15,552
can I not go to New York now?

268
00:18:15,553 --> 00:18:17,138
I want to take a break
from school.

269
00:18:22,393 --> 00:18:23,644
But why?

270
00:18:28,274 --> 00:18:30,067
There are other things
that I want to do.

271
00:18:30,192 --> 00:18:31,736
[Chang Ta-chin]
Just listen to me.

272
00:18:34,238 --> 00:18:37,575
Finish school first.
Everything else can wait.

273
00:18:40,494 --> 00:18:42,413
[soft music playing]

274
00:18:45,374 --> 00:18:46,626
Is there anything else?

275
00:19:02,642 --> 00:19:05,644
Liv, take measurements
in the kitchen and
inventory the equipment.

276
00:19:05,645 --> 00:19:06,853
Yes, ma'am.

277
00:19:06,854 --> 00:19:09,899
[pensive music playing]

278
00:19:27,625 --> 00:19:28,834
[sighs]

279
00:19:28,959 --> 00:19:30,211
I don't get it.

280
00:19:33,756 --> 00:19:35,508
Do we really have to do this?

281
00:19:36,634 --> 00:19:38,636
I don't think
you want to drive them away.

282
00:19:45,810 --> 00:19:47,687
For Chang Xin, we have to.

283
00:19:52,441 --> 00:19:54,359
So, for Chang Xin,

284
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:56,445
you think whatever
my dad says is right?

285
00:20:04,829 --> 00:20:07,747
You need to see things
in the long run.

286
00:20:07,748 --> 00:20:12,712
If you don't persist,
all efforts will go in vain.
Right?

287
00:20:19,301 --> 00:20:20,678
[grunts]

288
00:20:23,347 --> 00:20:25,725
I have faith
in your dad's decisions.

289
00:20:27,435 --> 00:20:28,602
[chuckles]

290
00:20:30,730 --> 00:20:33,482
Liv, give me the tablet.

291
00:20:35,943 --> 00:20:38,695
[Chang Xin manager]
This concludes this quarter's
store operations report.

292
00:20:38,696 --> 00:20:40,740
That's all from me, sir.

293
00:20:40,865 --> 00:20:41,906
[Chang Ta-chin] Good.

294
00:20:41,907 --> 00:20:44,576
You've all heard that.

295
00:20:44,577 --> 00:20:46,370
If you have any thoughts,

296
00:20:46,495 --> 00:20:48,372
let's bring them
to the table for discussion.

297
00:20:58,883 --> 00:21:01,469
If there's nothing,
that's it for today's meeting.

298
00:21:02,470 --> 00:21:03,554
Sir?

299
00:21:05,306 --> 00:21:06,724
I have a question.

300
00:21:11,312 --> 00:21:13,898
As for the series
of storefront purchases lately,

301
00:21:14,899 --> 00:21:16,484
I'd like to know
if it's necessary.

302
00:21:17,860 --> 00:21:19,320
What do you want to gain?

303
00:21:20,738 --> 00:21:22,031
I think it's good.

304
00:21:22,281 --> 00:21:24,074
We've purchased
so many storefronts
in a short time.

305
00:21:24,325 --> 00:21:25,742
Couldn't there be a problem?

306
00:21:25,743 --> 00:21:27,786
Is such a hasty purchase plan
really rational?

307
00:21:27,787 --> 00:21:30,748
Didn't the chairman tell us that
because of our expansion plan,

308
00:21:30,873 --> 00:21:33,626
we have to grab
any good storefront
that hits the market.

309
00:21:33,751 --> 00:21:35,753
But it doesn't make sense
from our perspective.

310
00:21:35,878 --> 00:21:37,504
We're still
in the early stages of the plan

311
00:21:37,505 --> 00:21:39,256
and we've already purchased
so many storefronts.

312
00:21:39,381 --> 00:21:40,966
Don't we need to slow down?

313
00:21:41,091 --> 00:21:43,302
Damn! Slow down for what?

314
00:21:43,427 --> 00:21:46,054
Now is the perfect time
to flex our muscles,

315
00:21:46,055 --> 00:21:49,015
so that the market will be
more confident in Chang Xin

316
00:21:49,016 --> 00:21:51,434
and everyone will invest in us,
and our stock price will go up.

317
00:21:51,435 --> 00:21:53,062
- It's as simple as that.
- You're so confident?

318
00:21:53,312 --> 00:21:55,815
Of course,
please look at this from
the strategic point of view...

319
00:21:55,940 --> 00:21:57,899
If you call this
preemptive preparation,
it's too preemptive.

320
00:21:57,900 --> 00:22:00,527
I told you
to look at this from
the strategic point of view.

321
00:22:00,528 --> 00:22:02,529
I thought you did well
in school.
What the hell have you learned?

322
00:22:02,530 --> 00:22:05,490
Sir? I suggest
you think twice about
purchasing more storefronts.

323
00:22:05,491 --> 00:22:06,826
The cost of purchasing
is too high.

324
00:22:06,951 --> 00:22:08,744
And we haven't done enough
customer traffic assessment.

325
00:22:09,787 --> 00:22:11,455
[Hsiu-wen]
Thanks for the reminder.

326
00:22:13,833 --> 00:22:15,835
Everything is going
according to plan.

327
00:22:15,960 --> 00:22:18,003
We don't need to slow
anything down.

328
00:22:18,128 --> 00:22:20,631
[tense music playing]

329
00:22:20,756 --> 00:22:21,924
[Chien-yuan] Hear that?

330
00:22:23,926 --> 00:22:27,680
Sir, there's no problem
with the purchase plan.

331
00:22:30,474 --> 00:22:31,517
Okay.

332
00:22:42,945 --> 00:22:45,781
[dramatic music playing]

333
00:22:48,492 --> 00:22:49,869
[elevator dings]

334
00:22:53,747 --> 00:22:54,874
- [Yu-li] Hi, there.
- Hi.

335
00:22:54,999 --> 00:22:57,418
[indistinct PA announcement]

336
00:23:04,049 --> 00:23:06,926
[Yu-li] Hi, Granny.
The calla lilies
are beautiful today.

337
00:23:06,927 --> 00:23:08,053
I think you'd love them.

338
00:23:26,697 --> 00:23:28,781
Feeling better?

339
00:23:28,782 --> 00:23:30,074
I'll give you a massage.

340
00:23:30,075 --> 00:23:31,785
Give me a five-star rating, okay?

341
00:23:34,955 --> 00:23:37,041
You're lucky I'm free today.

342
00:23:37,166 --> 00:23:41,921
Oh, thank you so much.
What would I do without you?

343
00:23:42,046 --> 00:23:44,548
- It's heavy.
- [Yu-li] Leave it there.

344
00:23:44,673 --> 00:23:46,467
I'll treat you to a meal.

345
00:23:51,513 --> 00:23:53,557
How's your granny?

346
00:23:53,682 --> 00:23:55,058
[Yu-li] Like this.

347
00:23:55,059 --> 00:23:57,645
I'm giving her a massage.
Maybe she'll feel better.

348
00:24:07,112 --> 00:24:08,155
Pst.

349
00:24:09,573 --> 00:24:12,116
- Putting on makeup
for a dead body.
- Don't be rude.

350
00:24:12,117 --> 00:24:14,453
He's new here. I'll say hello.

351
00:24:16,246 --> 00:24:19,165
Hi.

352
00:24:19,166 --> 00:24:21,084
[Yu-li] You're new here.

353
00:24:21,085 --> 00:24:23,837
Yeah. He used to be downstairs.
Just got moved up.

354
00:24:25,589 --> 00:24:27,632
Is this your son?

355
00:24:27,633 --> 00:24:28,968
[Wen] Yeah.

356
00:24:29,093 --> 00:24:33,097
It's his birthday. I'd like
to put on makeup for him.

357
00:24:34,932 --> 00:24:36,642
[Yu-li] How I envy your son!

358
00:24:38,185 --> 00:24:39,770
When I was younger,

359
00:24:39,895 --> 00:24:42,564
I had to put on makeup
or buy dresses in secret.

360
00:24:43,607 --> 00:24:46,235
[soft music playing]

361
00:24:46,485 --> 00:24:48,236
[Yu-li] Need my help?

362
00:24:48,237 --> 00:24:51,614
- Do you know how?
- I'm a pro.

363
00:24:51,615 --> 00:24:54,743
[Yu-li] No. I'll use mine.

364
00:24:59,164 --> 00:25:00,749
Here goes.

365
00:25:02,042 --> 00:25:05,838
He has fair skin, so heavy blush
and lipstick don't suit him.

366
00:25:05,963 --> 00:25:07,589
I'll spread it out.

367
00:25:08,841 --> 00:25:12,010
Next time,
before applying foundation,
put on some primer and cream.

368
00:25:12,011 --> 00:25:13,553
It's better for his skin.

369
00:25:13,554 --> 00:25:14,722
Okay.

370
00:25:18,058 --> 00:25:20,978
My granny loved
seeing me look pretty.

371
00:25:21,103 --> 00:25:24,023
I'm sure she'd love seeing me
make others look pretty.

372
00:25:27,651 --> 00:25:29,028
Happy birthday.

373
00:25:35,034 --> 00:25:37,286
[Tina] <i>Nowadays, in Taiwan,</i>

374
00:25:37,536 --> 00:25:41,165
a boy like Yu-chih
would have an easier time.

375
00:25:41,290 --> 00:25:44,126
[light jazz playing]

376
00:25:47,212 --> 00:25:51,175
Back then, I really wanted
to find out and punish the brat
who messed with him.

377
00:25:51,300 --> 00:25:55,011
How the hell could he push
a classmate down the stairs?

378
00:25:55,012 --> 00:25:57,014
That son of a bitch!

379
00:25:57,139 --> 00:25:59,224
Yu-chih was so unlucky.

380
00:26:05,689 --> 00:26:07,066
Come on.

381
00:26:07,191 --> 00:26:09,025
Don't think about it.

382
00:26:09,026 --> 00:26:10,193
Here.

383
00:26:10,194 --> 00:26:11,320
This one's on me.

384
00:26:26,710 --> 00:26:28,087
- Welcome!
- Cool!

385
00:26:28,212 --> 00:26:29,212
Take a photo.

386
00:26:29,213 --> 00:26:30,923
- Boss?
- Look here.

387
00:26:31,590 --> 00:26:32,716
[camera clicks]

388
00:26:34,885 --> 00:26:36,219
- Not bad, huh?
- What do you think?

389
00:26:36,220 --> 00:26:38,055
- Is it okay?
- Yes.

390
00:26:39,264 --> 00:26:40,766
It's great.

391
00:26:40,891 --> 00:26:43,268
[singer singing in Mandarin]

392
00:27:00,744 --> 00:27:01,995
Done.

393
00:27:02,996 --> 00:27:05,290
- How's that?
- Mm-hmm.

394
00:27:05,415 --> 00:27:07,709
[song continues]

395
00:27:18,262 --> 00:27:20,304
- Here we go.
- Finished?

396
00:27:20,305 --> 00:27:22,975
- [Chin-nan] Smells great.
- [Yu-li] Ta-da!

397
00:27:25,269 --> 00:27:28,312
- Taste it.
- [Feng] Let me try.

398
00:27:28,313 --> 00:27:30,190
- You first, Feng.
- Thank you.

399
00:27:32,943 --> 00:27:35,112
- Have a taste.
- It's hot.

400
00:27:37,281 --> 00:27:41,118
I think it should be spicier
to go with drinks.

401
00:27:41,243 --> 00:27:42,786
- Spicier?
- Yeah.

402
00:27:43,912 --> 00:27:45,872
It's spicy enough.

403
00:27:45,873 --> 00:27:47,457
Not enough. I mean it.

404
00:27:47,708 --> 00:27:49,126
Spicy enough.

405
00:27:49,251 --> 00:27:51,210
- Do I have to make it hotter?
- Yeah.

406
00:27:51,211 --> 00:27:52,838
Spicy enough.

407
00:27:52,963 --> 00:27:54,797
<i>Hello. It's me again,
Queen of Reviews.</i>

408
00:27:54,798 --> 00:27:56,132
<i>Jin Lai Hao serves up
the best Taiwanese flavor.</i>

409
00:27:56,133 --> 00:27:57,467
<i>To be honest,</i>

410
00:27:57,885 --> 00:27:59,844
<i>we've been through
a lot of setbacks lately.</i>

411
00:27:59,845 --> 00:28:01,888
<i>But nothing can stop us.</i>

412
00:28:01,889 --> 00:28:04,015
<i>If life is always
smooth sailing,
it is no fun, right?</i>

413
00:28:04,016 --> 00:28:07,644
<i>So, Jin Lai Hao is coming
back with a brand new look.</i>

414
00:28:07,769 --> 00:28:10,689
<i>Hey! This is Lin Chin-nan,
the pride of Jin Lai.</i>

415
00:28:10,814 --> 00:28:11,857
<i>Feng.</i>

416
00:28:11,982 --> 00:28:13,192
[clamoring]

417
00:28:13,317 --> 00:28:15,067
<i>- Am I on camera?
- Yeah.</i>

418
00:28:15,068 --> 00:28:17,403
<i>I don't look good,
but my food tastes good.</i>

419
00:28:17,404 --> 00:28:18,905
<i>That's a gentle guy.</i>

420
00:28:18,906 --> 00:28:21,073
<i>Yu-li, Goddess of Fire.</i>

421
00:28:21,074 --> 00:28:23,660
<i>Hello, this is Yu-li.
Come and taste my cocktails.</i>

422
00:28:23,785 --> 00:28:24,995
<i>Our boss.</i>

423
00:28:25,996 --> 00:28:27,872
<i>How do you like it here?</i>

424
00:28:27,873 --> 00:28:29,415
<i>Are you...</i>

425
00:28:29,416 --> 00:28:30,834
[Yi-hsuan] <i>He doesn't know
we're filming him.</i>

426
00:28:31,084 --> 00:28:32,169
<i>So many people came out
to support us today.</i>

427
00:28:32,294 --> 00:28:34,045
<i>Hello!</i>

428
00:28:34,046 --> 00:28:35,505
<i>We're your fans.</i>

429
00:28:35,756 --> 00:28:37,256
<i>- Really?
- Tell them what you think.</i>

430
00:28:37,257 --> 00:28:39,091
<i>I love the braised pork.
It's very special.</i>

431
00:28:39,092 --> 00:28:40,885
<i>Thank you. I mean it.</i>

432
00:28:40,886 --> 00:28:42,845
<i>As people who serve food,
we love hearing that.</i>

433
00:28:42,846 --> 00:28:45,014
<i>Thanks for your support.</i>

434
00:28:45,015 --> 00:28:46,225
<i>It tastes superb.</i>

435
00:28:46,350 --> 00:28:47,892
<i>- Come and get it.
- Thank you.</i>

436
00:28:47,893 --> 00:28:50,020
<i>You've ordered
our signature dish.</i>

437
00:28:50,145 --> 00:28:51,854
<i>I've been following you
since the days when you had
a storefront.</i>

438
00:28:51,855 --> 00:28:53,022
<i>- Really?
- Yeah.</i>

439
00:28:53,023 --> 00:28:54,399
<i>This is my business card.</i>

440
00:28:54,524 --> 00:28:56,068
<i>- Please come on our show.
- Please come.</i>

441
00:28:57,444 --> 00:28:58,945
<i>We've been...
Are you a producer?</i>

442
00:28:58,946 --> 00:29:00,030
<i>Yes.</i>

443
00:29:00,155 --> 00:29:02,114
<i>...noticed.
Oh, my God!</i>

444
00:29:02,115 --> 00:29:05,369
<i>I'm really happy
because getting ready for all
this wasn't easy at all.</i>

445
00:29:05,494 --> 00:29:07,286
<i>We're so busy and you've
been livestreaming.</i>

446
00:29:07,287 --> 00:29:08,204
<i>Don't you need to help us?</i>

447
00:29:08,205 --> 00:29:10,122
<i>You're here.</i>

448
00:29:10,123 --> 00:29:12,542
<i>Come to our food truck.
Grab a bite to eat.</i>

449
00:29:12,793 --> 00:29:16,380
[narrator] <i>Hey guys,
the new season
of</i> Super Chef <i>is back.</i>

450
00:29:16,755 --> 00:29:18,256
<i>We want to blow everyone away
with Taiwanese cuisine.</i>

451
00:29:18,257 --> 00:29:19,966
<i>Come sign up
for the auditions.</i>

452
00:29:19,967 --> 00:29:21,218
<i>Turn braised pork rice
into a Michelin dish</i>

453
00:29:21,385 --> 00:29:23,345
<i>and bring home
the million-dollar prize.</i>

454
00:29:23,762 --> 00:29:26,472
<i>Sign up now and start
the Taiwanese cuisine
revolution.</i>

455
00:29:26,473 --> 00:29:29,059
It's cool.
We'll be on television.

456
00:29:29,184 --> 00:29:32,938
Right. Cooking is a show.
This is the direction
we're going in.

457
00:29:33,063 --> 00:29:35,941
[Feng] How are we
supposed to sign up?

458
00:29:36,066 --> 00:29:38,067
We don't own a restaurant,
just a food truck.

459
00:29:38,068 --> 00:29:42,321
Because we're a food truck,
we're special, a gimmick
for their show.

460
00:29:42,322 --> 00:29:44,490
A food truck versus restaurants.

461
00:29:44,491 --> 00:29:47,493
It'd be great if we win,
but it's alright if we lose,

462
00:29:47,494 --> 00:29:50,997
because we still
get more exposure.

463
00:29:50,998 --> 00:29:53,375
I love the idea.
It doesn't matter
whether we win or lose.

464
00:29:53,500 --> 00:29:55,167
It's all about getting exposure.

465
00:29:55,168 --> 00:29:57,587
Hey. Contestants must be
in mixed-gender pairs.

466
00:29:57,838 --> 00:29:59,298
Damn, we're a shoo-in.

467
00:30:00,173 --> 00:30:02,091
We have them.

468
00:30:02,092 --> 00:30:03,427
Yeah, we have them.

469
00:30:04,344 --> 00:30:05,929
I can try.

470
00:30:08,932 --> 00:30:11,435
I think it's a bit high-profile.

471
00:30:13,353 --> 00:30:15,814
But you're already
one of our popular chefs.

472
00:30:16,857 --> 00:30:20,526
I mean, our target audience
is young people
and nine-to-fivers in Taipei.

473
00:30:20,527 --> 00:30:22,237
Going on television...

474
00:30:23,447 --> 00:30:25,115
I'll think about it.

475
00:30:31,955 --> 00:30:34,041
Forget it. I'll try.

476
00:30:35,125 --> 00:30:37,336
I'll be your partner.

477
00:30:37,461 --> 00:30:39,462
But you can't cook.

478
00:30:39,463 --> 00:30:41,547
I'll use my mouth,
and you'll do the work.

479
00:30:41,548 --> 00:30:42,966
[Feng] Come on.

480
00:30:43,091 --> 00:30:44,801
Stop joking around.

481
00:30:44,926 --> 00:30:48,137
Maybe I'll dress up as a girl.
I can chop fast.

482
00:30:48,138 --> 00:30:51,140
No. Wait.
You dress up as a girl?

483
00:30:51,141 --> 00:30:52,558
Why don't we just give up?

484
00:30:52,559 --> 00:30:54,019
The point is that
we'll be on TV.

485
00:30:54,144 --> 00:30:55,936
As far as cooking is concerned,
I'm better than you.

486
00:30:55,937 --> 00:30:57,981
- [Chin-nan] So,
you'll dress up as a girl?
- [Feng] So what?

487
00:30:58,106 --> 00:31:00,149
[Chin-nan] Damn, are you sure
you can look good if you dress
up as a girl? Come on.

488
00:31:00,150 --> 00:31:02,109
It doesn't matter
if I'll look good.

489
00:31:02,110 --> 00:31:05,279
[Chin-nan]
If you dress up as a girl,
the audience might throw up.

490
00:31:05,280 --> 00:31:07,199
[Feng]
It's a cooking competition,
not a beauty contest.

491
00:31:07,324 --> 00:31:08,825
Do you think you can look good
if you dress up as a girl?

492
00:31:08,950 --> 00:31:11,077
- I can.
- Like hell you can.

493
00:31:11,078 --> 00:31:12,621
- You'd only look good
in your burial clothes.
- Go cook at a funeral home.

494
00:31:12,871 --> 00:31:14,372
- At least, I'm young.
- Enough!

495
00:31:14,373 --> 00:31:15,624
[Feng] You'll cook
at a funeral home.

496
00:31:15,874 --> 00:31:17,042
[Yu-li] That's enough!

497
00:31:19,336 --> 00:31:21,088
I'm just worried
I'll hold you back.

498
00:31:23,673 --> 00:31:25,342
You can do it.

499
00:31:32,057 --> 00:31:35,059
- Fine. I'll try.
- Got her. Reverse psychology.

500
00:31:35,060 --> 00:31:36,853
- Hey, you...
- Reverse psychology.

501
00:31:36,978 --> 00:31:38,230
Got her!

502
00:31:39,022 --> 00:31:41,942
I want people to see
our cooking again, okay?

503
00:31:44,027 --> 00:31:45,570
Okay. Let's do this.

504
00:31:50,075 --> 00:31:52,077
- Jin Lai Hao, three, two, one!
- Go!

505
00:31:52,202 --> 00:31:53,954
You can do it.

506
00:31:57,624 --> 00:31:59,584
Dad, I'd like
to tell you something.

507
00:31:59,709 --> 00:32:02,128
One of my friends
is a TV show producer.

508
00:32:02,129 --> 00:32:04,923
He's preparing
for a cooking competition show.

509
00:32:05,048 --> 00:32:08,217
Although Chang Xin is already
a sponsor of the show,

510
00:32:08,218 --> 00:32:13,557
I was wondering,
if we participate
in the competition,

511
00:32:13,682 --> 00:32:16,393
that it'll be good
for our visibility.

512
00:32:17,060 --> 00:32:19,062
[pensive music playing]

513
00:32:24,401 --> 00:32:26,403
What if we lose?

514
00:32:26,528 --> 00:32:28,071
No, we won't.

515
00:32:28,196 --> 00:32:30,073
I'm definitely going to win.

516
00:32:40,417 --> 00:32:42,335
Sorry. I'll come back later.

517
00:32:43,587 --> 00:32:46,297
Hsiu-wen? Come here.

518
00:32:46,298 --> 00:32:48,132
Let me see that.

519
00:32:48,133 --> 00:32:49,009
Yes, sir.

520
00:32:57,976 --> 00:33:01,521
[Yi-hsuan]
<i>I have something sad
to announce today.</i>

521
00:33:01,688 --> 00:33:05,108
<i>Because of a hostile
takeover of our storefront
by a large enterprise,</i>

522
00:33:05,233 --> 00:33:07,611
<i>our Jin Lai Hao
is forced to close down.</i>

523
00:33:07,736 --> 00:33:10,696
<i>However, don't be sad
for too long, guys.</i>

524
00:33:10,697 --> 00:33:12,364
<i>We'll return soon.</i>

525
00:33:12,365 --> 00:33:14,658
Where are they opening
their new restaurant?

526
00:33:14,659 --> 00:33:16,495
They're running
a food truck business.

527
00:33:16,620 --> 00:33:18,121
- A food truck?
- [Hsiu-wen] Yeah.

528
00:33:18,246 --> 00:33:20,289
They're very popular
on the Internet.

529
00:33:20,290 --> 00:33:23,501
They've been running
around Taipei and taken part
in many pop-up events.

530
00:33:23,502 --> 00:33:25,503
Many young people love them.

531
00:33:25,504 --> 00:33:28,965
From looking for a truck,
to every detail
of the decoration,

532
00:33:29,090 --> 00:33:31,550
they've documented
and shared it all online.

533
00:33:31,551 --> 00:33:34,220
Many trendy young people
who want to start
their own business

534
00:33:34,221 --> 00:33:35,805
really relate to them.

535
00:33:36,056 --> 00:33:39,518
They're even more popular online
than they used to be.

536
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:45,482
Whose idea?

537
00:33:48,527 --> 00:33:52,280
I don't think
it was Chou Lu-yung.
I think it was Chao Yi-hsuan.

538
00:33:53,323 --> 00:33:55,116
[Chang Ta-chin] Chao Yi-hsuan?

539
00:34:03,708 --> 00:34:08,338
What do you think
about Jin Lai Hao
without Chao Yi-hsuan?

540
00:34:09,381 --> 00:34:11,508
Then we'd have nothing
to worry about.

541
00:34:16,763 --> 00:34:19,640
[Chang Ta-chin] Hsiu-wen,
when the acquisition is done,

542
00:34:19,641 --> 00:34:23,687
go help Chien-yuan get ready
for the cooking competition.

543
00:34:23,812 --> 00:34:25,688
Yes, sir.

544
00:34:25,689 --> 00:34:28,567
No need, Dad. I've got this.

545
00:34:28,692 --> 00:34:31,235
Don't worry.
I'll do a great job.

546
00:34:31,236 --> 00:34:32,571
It's you I'm worried about.

547
00:34:34,281 --> 00:34:36,616
With Hsiu-wen's help,
I can rest easy.

548
00:34:47,460 --> 00:34:50,505
[credits music playing]
